CLASSIFIED



Item #: SCP-5458



Euclid




~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~



SCP-5458 taken at [REDACTED]



Special Containment Procedures: 

SCP-5458 is to be contained in an 8m x 4m x 4m air-tight, steel cell. A ventilator and a tube connecting to a hydrogen chloride (HCL) tank are needed in the cell. Surveillance cameras and a thermometer are also to be installed. The enclosure must not have any sources that could change the cell's temperature except for SCP-5458 itself. The cell also must have an air-tight vestibule door.

Anyone who enters the cell must wear air-tight clothing and a gas mask; no skin can be exposed. The SCP-5458-1 neutralization procedures also need to take place every five days.

Description: 

SCP-5458 is an anomalous Brunswick piano currently kept at Site-█. SCP-5458 must be constantly performed without any mistakes made when played. If any of this is violated, a transparent gas capable of corroding through human flesh will be released from the back of SCP-5458 within 20 seconds. The gas is classified as SCP-5458-1.

SCP-5458-1 can be produced infinitely by SCP-5458; it is currently impossible to find the cause of the production, and it is impossible to stop the production permanently.

According to the results of experiments tested on D-Class subjects by Doctor ██████, when exposing a human to SCP-5458-1 without any protective clothing, the subject will die within 2 - 5 minutes due to blood loss if not treated properly and 10 - 25 seconds if inhaled, making the gas very dangerous to humans. It is also tested that when SCP-5458-1 is released, it will significantly increase the surrounding environment's temperature. This can be used to detect SCP-5458-1's presence.

SCP-5458-1 cannot be destroyed but can be neutralized into SCP-5458-2 when reacted with hydrogen chloride. SCP-5458-2 is not corrosive, nor does it have any adverse effects on humans. SCP-5458-2 is usually ventilated out of the building after the SCP-5458-1 neutralization procedure is complete. Interestingly, SCP-5458-2 is weighed to be 1.29 times lighter than hydrogen gas, which is an anomaly thought to be scientifically impossible.

SCP-5458-1 Neutralization Procedures: 

Bleach will first be applied onto SCP-5458 to protect the entity from any corrosion of the chemicals. 108L of hydrogen chloride will then be released into the cell. It will take approximately 5 minutes for the hydrogen chloride to neutralize all present SCP-5458-1. Extra hydrogen chloride is then to be released, and the cell is to be left for five additional minutes before ventilating all SCP-5458-2 and remaining hydrogen chloride out of the building. Fresh air will then be released back into the cell.

Discovery and Investigation: 

SCP-5458 was first located in an abandoned house in ████ ██████, Israel. It was found in a basement with four human remains and an old man performing on the entity. SCP-5458 was seized during an MTF Beta-7 () raid when three residents and a local policeman were reported missing after exploring the house. An MTF agent (B7-3) and the old man were both killed due to contact with SCP-5458-1.

After a thorough investigation of the house, traces of a cult named  were found. Ethnicity DNA tests from bloodstains also lead to an Israeli village called Quaal. MTF agents searched Quaal for the cult. However, no traces were found except a book titled «Testaments of Isaiah Lebar».

